    "result_text": "The change is complete. The full build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires rejecting a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a **400**.\n\n**What I found:**\n- `registrationDate` is a `LocalDate` on the `Owner` model, defaulting to the server's current date when not supplied (`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`).\n- The request DTOs are **generated from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** by the OpenAPI generator.\n- The codebase already validates other fields (email, telephone) by attaching jakarta Bean Validation constraints via `x-field-extra-annotation`, which flow through `@Valid` on the generated controller interface and are mapped to **400** by `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`.\n\n**The fix** (one edit, `openapi.yml`): added `@jakarta.validation.constraints.PastOrPresent` to the `registrationDate` field. \"Not later than the server date\" is exactly *past-or-present*, and `@PastOrPresent` operates on `LocalDate` against the current date. A future date now produces a `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400, while an unsupplied date (null) is skipped by the constraint and still defaults to the server date.\n\nThis reuses the existing validation-and-error-mapping machinery rather than adding a new code path, keeping the logic where it belongs (declarative field constraint in the schema, alongside the other field validations).",
